From 6f2c3cc87e7fa437ff6258504e745699b7acc114 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:14:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(post): ship an example starter set on the Sodick ALC400G

The built-in Sodick ALC400G stated no EDM condition, guide heights or
threader, so each Wire Contour was refused until the user wrote a .mch.
The file now states three example conditions (C110 rough, C120 skim,
C130 finish, 0.25 mm wire), example guide heights 0 / 130 mm and
awt: true. Each row and the description say EXAMPLE - replace. The EDM
guide page says how to replace them with the control's own table.

Fixes #3214

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
